  <section class="cp-faq-section cp-screen-only" aria-labelledby="cp-faq-title"><div class="cp-wrap cp-faq-grid"><div><p class="cp-eyebrow">Know what you are getting</p><h2 id="cp-faq-title">A practical preview.<br>Clear next steps.</h2><p>Use the planner to explore an approach, then bring the details of your business into the conversation.</p></div><div class="cp-faq-list">
    <details><summary>What does the free B2B outbound campaign planner do?</summary><p>It matches your offer, industry, buyer, region and goal to prepared CallTeam guidance. The preview gives you a starting approach for the audience, conversation and qualification, with related resources to explore.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Is this a researched campaign for my company?</summary><p>The preview is based on the answers you select. It does not inspect your website, verify your capabilities or research individual target accounts. We develop that company-specific context when discussing a real campaign.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What if my offer or industry does not have a close match?</summary><p>The planner uses a broader approach and makes the limits clear when a specific match is unavailable. Choose the nearest honest category, or select the other-offer option. Bring the details to CallTeam so we can assess the market properly.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can I use the opening and qualification questions?</summary><p>Yes. Adapt them to your actual offer, buyer and evidence before using them. Replace placeholders, verify any company-specific references and keep product claims within what your team can support.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Does the preview include a prospect list or promise meetings?</summary><p>It provides planning guidance and a conversation starting point. Account research, contact data, campaign capacity, meeting standards and expected outcomes need a separate scope discussion.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What happens when I send the preview or book a call?</summary><p>We review your offer, target market, current sales process and the approach you selected. Then we discuss the research, calling, qualification and follow-up required, and whether CallTeam fits the work.</p></details>
